# Game Enhancement Specifications (Multi-Game)

---

## Sliding-Puzzle Enhancements

### Task: Three User-Friendliness Upgrades

Add three user-friendliness upgrades to sliding-puzzle — orientation, forgiveness, momentum. No changes to core.js shuffle/scoring/solvability, or the campaign/library/multiplayer roadmap.

---

#### 1) CAMPAIGN STAGE PREVIEW (hub → stage grid)

Players tapping a locked/unlocked stage node currently only see lock-state + stars —
no idea what they're walking into (grid size, par time/moves) until they start.

**Behavior:**
- On tap/focus of a stage node (locked or unlocked), show a small inline preview
  panel (not a new screen): grid size (e.g. "4×4"), par time, par moves, and whether
  it's a numbers or picture round.
- Locked nodes show the same preview plus the unlock requirement ("Clear Stage 6
  to unlock"), never a blank/mystery card.
- Pull this data straight from `levels.js` stage definitions — no new data, just
  surfacing fields that already exist.

---

#### 2) "ALMOST THERE" NUDGE ON WRONG-TILE SHAKE

The shake animation on an illegal move currently gives no sense of proximity — a
one-tile-off near-solve and a totally scrambled board feel identical.

**Implementation:**
- No new detection logic: reuse the existing board state to check "is exactly one
  pair of tiles swapped from solved" (a cheap O(n) scan already implementable from
  the board array core.js exposes) — if true, show a subtle one-time-per-round
  banner "So close! One swap away." instead of the plain shake.
- Only fires once per round (first time the condition is true), never nags on every
  move — track with a per-round in-memory flag, not persisted storage.
- Numbers mode only; skip for picture mode where "one swap away" isn't visually
  obvious the same way.

---

#### 3) RESUME BANNER CLARITY

Resume already snapshots `{size, seed?, board, moves, playedMs, mode, assists,
stageId?}` — but per the spec a returning player just sees a bare "Continue"
control with no context on what they're resuming.

**Implementation:**
- Expand the Continue affordance (menu hub) to show: grid size, elapsed time so
  far, move count, and — if `stageId` is set — the stage name/number, so resuming a
  campaign stage reads differently from resuming free play.
- If the resume snapshot is stale (e.g. corrupted/partial per the existing
  guarded-read contract), fail exactly as today (silently drop it) — this only
  changes what's *shown* when a valid snapshot exists, not the resume logic itself.

---

#### Testing

Extend the existing jest suite:

- **Stage-preview data lookup:** Returns correct fields for a known stageId (locked and unlocked)
- **One-swap-away detector:** True only for exactly one transposition from solved, false for solved itself and for 2+ swaps away
- **Resume-banner field mapping:** From a snapshot fixture (incl. stageId present vs absent) — no changes to snapshot save/restore behavior itself

