## Word-Puzzle Enhancements

### Task: Three User-Friendliness Upgrades

Add three user-friendliness upgrades to word-puzzle — visibility, confidence, momentum. No changes to core.js generator, matching logic, or star thresholds.

---

#### 1) LIVE DIRECTION FEEDBACK DURING DRAG

Players currently only find out a drag was invalid (wrong direction / non-collinear)
when they release and get the red flash — no feedback while dragging.

**Implementation:**
- While `pointermove` is sampling cells, if the current path from anchor to cursor
  is NOT one of the tier's 8 direction vectors in a straight line (i.e. `lineCells`
  would return null for the in-progress path), show a subtle "invalid direction"
  visual state on the live highlight (e.g. desaturated/dashed instead of solid),
  distinct from the normal in-progress highlight and from the release-time red flash.
- The moment the path becomes a valid straight line again, the highlight returns to
  normal. This is presentation only — call the same `lineCells` check already used
  at release-time, just also on each pointermove sample; no new matching logic.

---

#### 2) HINT-USE CLARITY FOR STAR LOSS

" hintsUsed === 0 && wrongPicks ≤ 2" is invisible to the player in the moment —
using a hint silently costs a star with no feedback until the result overlay.

**Implementation:**
- The first time a player taps [Hint] in a level (not every time — first use per
  level only), show a brief one-time toast: "Using a hint means no perfect-run star
  this level." Track via a session/in-memory flag (per level attempt), not new
  persisted storage — this is a one-time-per-attempt heads up, not a nag.
- No change to the actual star math in `starsFor` — copy-only, sourced from
  config.js strings (same override chain as existing copy).

---

#### 3) THEME-COMPLETE MOMENTUM → NEXT THEME

Per the spec, theme-complete shows a badge but the flow doesn't clearly point
toward what's next — players who finish a theme may not realize there are 3 more.

**Implementation:**
- On the theme-complete overlay, in addition to the badge, show a compact strip of
  the OTHER themes with their current star totals (x/9) so the "one more theme"
  pull is visible immediately, not buried back on the menu.
- Tapping a theme in that strip goes straight into its first unstarted level (or
  level 1 if none started) — same navigation the menu cards already support, just
  reachable one tap earlier from the completion moment.

---

#### Testing

Extend the existing jest suite:

- **Live-direction validity check:** Reuses `lineCells` and matches release-time validity for the same path (no drift between live and final checks)
- **Hint-toast fires only on first hint tap per level attempt** (session-scoped, not persisted)
- **Theme-complete strip data:** Star totals per theme match `progress` storage for a fixture save

